  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Visitors can observe objects and record brief responses on a printed activity sheet.\", \"decision\": \"How should a self-guided activity use a printed prompt?\", \"goal\": \"Help visitors find a satisfying route through the museum while keeping reception and volunteers manageable.\", \"problem\": \"A volunteer-run local museum wants to make a weekend visit easier to navigate. It has a modest collection, printed guides, a reception table, flexible volunteer positions, and several rooms that can remain open independently. The decisions concern interpretation and visitor organization, not conservation rules or safety policy.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nThe sheet gives a prompt before each observation and asks for a response afterward. The prompt directs attention before visitors look closely.\nThe sheet pairs each prompt with a response space and lets visitors choose their own observation order. Visitors can organize the activity around their interests.\nThe sheet asks visitors to observe first, then reveals a prompt for their response. Initial noticing is left open before a focused reflection."
    }
  ],
